notes:
Space Traffic Management

A Space Traffic Management system
- is a concept similar to Air Traffic Control, but for satellites rather than planes.
- would aim to set up legal and ___ ways of improving safety.
- does not actually exist at present.

Problems in developing effective Space Traffic Management
- Satellites are now quite ___ and therefore more widespread (e.g. there are constellations made up of ___ of satellites).
- At present, satellites are not required to transmit information to help with their ___.
- There are few systems for ___ satellites.
- Small pieces of debris may be difficult to identify.
- Operators may be unwilling to share details of satellites used for ___ or commercial reasons.
- It may be hard to collect details of the object's ___ at a given time.
- Scientists can only make a ___ about where the satellite will go.

Solutions
- Common standards should be agreed on for the presentation of information.
- The information should be combined in one ___.
- A coordinated system must be designed to create ___ among its users.

